\v 18 \add While\add* he was still speaking¦232585, another \add messenger\add* came¦232587 and said¦232588, “Your¦232589 sons¦232589 and daughters¦232590 were¦232591 eating¦232591 and drinking¦232592 wine¦232593 in¦232594 the house¦232594 of their¦232595 eldest brother¦232595
\v 19 when \add suddenly\add* a \add freak\add* wind¦232599 came¦232601 from¦232603 across¦232603 the desert and struck¦232605 the house¦232608. It¦232609 \add collapsed\add* on¦232606 the young¦232612 people¦232612 and \add killed them\add*, and only¦232615 I¦232614 alone¦232618 have¦232614 escaped¦232614 to tell you.”
\p
\v 20 Then Iyyov¦232623 stood up¦232622 and tore¦232624 his robe¦232627 and shaved¦232628 his head¦232631. Then he knelt with his face to the ground and worshipped¦232634 \add God\add*,
